.TH CCOL_EVENT_LOOP_REG_COUNT 3 "2026-07-12" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
ccol_event_loop_reg_count \- number of currently-registered ccol_event_reg handles
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <cthreadcomm.h>

size_t ccol_event_loop_reg_count(ccol_event_loop loop);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Returns the number of live registrations (ccol_event_loop_add() calls not yet
removed), not the number of epoll interest-list entries: one fd with
both directions registered counts as 2, since it is backed by two
independent ccol_event_reg handles sharing one entry.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
loop  ccol_event_loop to query.
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
Returns the registration count on success.
Returns (size_t)-1 if loop is CCOL_EVENT_LOOP_INVALID or a stale/
already-destroyed handle.
.fi
.SH THREAD SAFETY
.nf
Safe to call concurrently with ccol_event_loop_add(), ccol_event_loop_remove(),
and dispatch on any reactor thread; returns a consistent snapshot (a
single atomic load, torn-read-free) rather than a value protected by any
lock.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR ccol_event_loop_add (3),
.BR ccol_event_loop_remove (3)
